  "label": "Islamophobia Stereotype",
  "description": "The meme implicitly relies on the stereotype that Muslims are incompatible with Western values or LGBTQ+ identities, often portraying them as 'backward' or threatening. This is reinforced by the juxtaposition of the niqab (a symbol of Islamic modesty) with the rainbow flag (a symbol of LGBTQ+ pride), suggesting a conflict or incompatibility between these identities. This stereotype is rooted in real-world Islamophobic discourse that frames Islam as inherently opposed to modern, liberal values.",
